-- V88: Backfill genuinely-missing/incomplete "Merkez"-pattern neighborhoods.
--
-- BACKGROUND (see V36/V37 for prior history — this migration does NOT
-- reintroduce what those removed):
--   V36/V37 deleted FAKE placeholder neighborhoods (gen_random_uuid(),
--   no polygon, arbitrary names like "Beykoz Merkez") seeded by V5/V6/V24
--   before real OSM boundaries existed. That cleanup was correct — those
--   rows had no real geometry and no real data.
--   V27 then imported real OSM administrative boundaries citywide, but at
--   that time OSM's Overpass data did not yet resolve a "Merkez" (or
--   "Ağva Merkez") administrative relation for Beykoz, Çekmeköy, Şile, and
--   Maltepe — so no replacement row was created for these specific real
--   mahalles. Districts ended up with zero DB row for a genuinely real,
--   currently-populated, government-registered mahalle.
--
-- EVIDENCE (2026-08-13 audit, scripts/audit_anatolian_geodata.py):
--   1. A fresh OSM Overpass fetch NOW resolves administrative boundaries
--      for all six mahalles below (OSM data has been completed/edited
--      since V27 ran) — geometry embedded here is exactly that fetch
--      result, cached at scripts/.audit_cache/<district>_ground_truth.json.
--   2. Independent cross-check against a second, non-OSM source — Turkey's
--      official TÜİK/İçişleri Bakanlığı neighborhood list, via
--      https://github.com/bertugfahriozer/il_ilce_mahalle (no polygon
--      data, names/hierarchy only, "processed from official neighborhood
--      lists") — confirms all six are real, currently-registered mahalles
--      of their respective districts:
--        BEYKOZ MERKEZ Mah., MERKEZ Mah. (Çekmeköy), AĞVA MERKEZ Mah.,
--        KÜÇÜKYALI MERKEZ Mah., and (space variant only) AŞAĞI DUDULLU /
--        YUKARI DUDULLU Mah. (Ümraniye).
--   3. Building impact: during this session's district building imports,
--      OSM-tagged buildings under these exact neighborhood names could
--      not match any DB row and were skipped entirely (never inserted):
--      Beykoz 1246, Çekmeköy 1729, Şile (Ağva Merkez) 177, Maltepe
--      (Küçükyalı Merkez) 985 — total 4137 buildings. A post-migration
--      reimport (idempotent, same ndjson files already in the repo)
--      picks these up.
--   4. Ümraniye's "Aşağıdudullu"/"Yukarıdudullu" rows already existed but
--      with NULL geometry and a no-space spelling that doesn't match OSM's
--      "Aşağı Dudullu"/"Yukarı Dudullu" — renamed + geometry backfilled
--      for map completeness. Both are 0-building areas in OSM's own
--      building fetch (an OSB/industrial-zone-adjacent area), consistent
--      across both fetch runs — not a building-assignment bug.
--
-- Ambiguous/unverified cases found in the same audit (Büyükada, Sedef
-- Adası, Anadoluhisarı spelling-duplicate, ~50 other cross-district
-- duplicate-name rows, etc.) are deliberately NOT touched here — see the
-- audit report for the full classification. Only entries with both (a) an
-- OSM boundary that resolves today and (b) independent official-source
-- confirmation are backfilled.

BEGIN;

-- New rows: districts with NO existing row at all for the real mahalle.
